# 9. MOCK DATA AND SERVICE ARCHITECTURE

This requirement is mandatory.

**Never hardcode mock data directly inside page components.**

Separate:
- Types.
- Mock data.
- Service interfaces.
- Mock service implementations.
- UI components.

For example:

```ts
export interface Repository {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  owner: string;
  url: string;
  branch: string;
  commitSha: string;
  language: string;
  framework: string[];
  status: "pending" | "analyzing" | "completed" | "failed";
  fileCount: number;
  lastAnalyzed: string;
}

export interface RepositoryService {
  getRepositories(): Promise<Repository[]>;
  getRepository(id: string): Promise<Repository>;
  addRepository(url: string): Promise<Repository>;
  deleteRepository(id: string): Promise<void>;
}
```

Create mock implementations separately.

For example:

```text
src/
  services/
    api/
      repository.service.ts
    mock/
      repository.mock.ts
      assistant.mock.ts
      architecture.mock.ts
      execution.mock.ts
      dependency.mock.ts
      documentation.mock.ts
```

Use a service abstraction that allows Phase 2 to replace mock services with real API services.

Do not make page components dependent on mock implementation details.

Use asynchronous mock responses where necessary to simulate realistic loading states.

